<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Our Taping & Jointing Services</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Taping and jointing is the modern alternative to wet plastering. Instead of applying wet plaster over plasterboard joints, our skilled technicians apply jointing compound and paper tape to create an invisible, crack-resistant seam. The result is a perfectly smooth wall or ceiling that is ready for painting or wallpapering in a fraction of the time.</p>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Edinburgh's property market — from new build apartments in the Leith Waterfront and Fountainbridge to loft conversions in Stockbridge, office refurbishments in the New Town, and residential extensions in Morningside and Bruntsfield — demands finishers who can deliver flawless results quickly and cleanly. Our team uses professional-grade jointing compounds from British Gypsum (Gyproc) and Knauf, delivering finishes that meet the highest quality standards across all Edinburgh projects. Whether you're finishing a single room in a Victorian tenement on King Street or taping and jointing an entire new development in the Edinburgh Enterprise Zone, we deliver consistent, professional results.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Inspect and prepare all board joints and screw holes</li>
  <li>Apply jointing tape and first coat of compound (embedding coat)</li>
  <li>Second coat for seamless blending over taped joints</li>
  <li>Third coat for final smoothing and feathered edges</li>
  <li>Sanding to a smooth, paint-ready finish using dust extraction</li>
  <li>Metal and flexible corner bead installation for crisp, durable edges</li>
  <li>Bulkhead and complex shape jointing for feature ceilings and cornices</li>
  <li>Final inspection and site cleanup before decoration handover</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Taping & Jointing?</h2>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li><strong>Faster than plastering:</strong> Taping and jointing is significantly faster than wet plastering, with no lengthy drying times. Rooms are ready for decoration in days, not weeks — important for Edinburgh's fast-moving property market and commercial projects with tight deadlines.</li>
  <li><strong>Cleaner process:</strong> Jointing compound produces minimal dust during application and no wet plaster mess. We use dust extraction for sanding to keep your Edinburgh property clean throughout the process.</li>
  <li><strong>Crack-resistant finish:</strong> Properly taped joints are flexible and move with the building, preventing the cracking that can occur as wet plaster dries and shrinks — particularly important for Edinburgh's older properties that experience natural settlement.</li>
  <li><strong>Cost-effective:</strong> Less labour and material than full plastering, making it ideal for large areas, multiple rooms, and commercial projects across Edinburgh.</li>
  <li><strong>Professional results:</strong> Our skilled finishers achieve a flawless surface that is indistinguishable from plastered walls and ready for painting or wallpapering, with the added benefit of no drying time waiting period.</li>
  <li><strong>Consistent quality:</strong> Unlike wet plastering which depends heavily on weather conditions and humidity, taping and jointing produces reliable results year-round regardless of Edinburgh's climate.</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Materials & Specifications</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">We use professional-grade materials from leading UK manufacturers to ensure a durable, crack-resistant finish on every Edinburgh project.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>British Gypsum Gyproc joint compound (All Purpose, Multi-Finish, TopCoat) and finishing products</li>
  <li>Knauf jointing systems — Knauf Rapid, Knauf TopCoat, and ready-mixed compounds</li>
  <li>Paper jointing tape for strong, flexible seams between boards</li>
  <li>Scrim tape for internal corners and board intersections</li>
  <li>Metal corner beads for crisp, durable external corners</li>
  <li>Flexible corner beads for curved and bulkhead details</li>
  <li>Dust extraction equipment for clean, residue-free sanding</li>
  <li>Protective sheeting for floors, furnishings, and Edinburgh property fixtures</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Applications & Use Cases</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our taping and jointing services are suitable for all types of drylined surfaces across Edinburgh and the Lothians.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
