<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Frequently Asked Questions about Taping & Jointing</h2>
<div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">What is taping and jointing?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Taping and jointing is the process of covering plasterboard joints and screw holes with jointing compound and paper tape. It creates a smooth, seamless finish ready for painting without the need for wet plastering.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">How long does taping and jointing take in Edinburgh?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">A typical room takes 2-3 days including drying time between coats. Larger projects in Edinburgh take proportionally longer, but the process is still faster than traditional wet plastering.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Is taping and jointing better than plastering?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Taping and jointing is faster, cleaner, and more cost-effective than wet plastering. It produces a smooth, crack-resistant finish that is indistinguishable from plastered walls and ready for decoration sooner.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Will the joints crack over time?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">When done correctly, taped joints are highly resistant to cracking. We use paper tape and multiple coats of jointing compound to create a flexible, durable seam that moves with the building.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Can you tape and joint ceilings as well as walls?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Yes. We provide taping and jointing for both walls and ceilings, including bulkheads, bulkhead details, and complex shapes.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Do I need to sand between coats?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">We handle all sanding between coats as part of our service. Our team uses dust extraction equipment to minimise mess and leaves your surfaces smooth and ready for painting.</p>
  </div>
